// Please add a file called ${SOURCE_FILE_NAME}.orig, which contains the original source code

This is the source file. It is a contract test file generated by Microsoft Pex and NUnit for ArrayList. It checks different methods of ArrayList, such as Add, Remove, Insert, Set, Get etc.

I get errors on the Microsoft.Pex.Framework and Microsoft.Pex.Framework.Exceptions namespaces, saying they cannot be found.  I guess these namespaces are part of the Microsoft.Pex.Framework. 

I tried to add the path of the 'Microsoft.Pex.Framework.dll' and 'Microsoft.Pex.Framework.Exceptions.dll' to the references of my project, and I am still facing the same issue.

I also tried creating a new Console Application project and added the mentioned namespaces.

I am using Visual Studio 2017 and targeting the .NET Framework version v4.7.2.

I'm not facing this issue with other projects which are using the same version of the Framework. Just this one, please help me.


A: The problem was solved when I upgraded the Visual Studio 2017. I did so by going to 


*

*help -> about

*I saw that I am running on 'Developer Preview 15.7.1'

*Go to -> about -> upgrade

*A modal window came up asking me if I want to upgrade. I clicked on "Yes".

*After the upgrade, Visual Studio restarted automatically.


After the upgrade, it worked perfectly for me without any issues.
Not sure if this is a bug with Visual Studio or what, but it seems like upgrading has fixed the issue.

